1. If the year is divisible by 4, it is a leap year, except for end-of-century years (years divisible by 100).
2. For end-of-century years, if the year is divisible by 400, it is a leap year; otherwise, it is not a leap year.

The function first checks if the year is divisible by 4 using the modulus operator `%`. If it is divisible by 4, it then checks if the year is divisible by 100. If it is divisible by 100, it further checks if the year is divisible by 400. If it is divisible by 400, it returns `True` (leap year), otherwise, it returns `False` (not a leap year). If the year is divisible by 4 but not by 100, it directly returns `True` (leap year). If the year is not divisible by 4, it returns `False` (not a leap year).

