The neighborhood also plays a crucial role in preserving and promoting Santiago's artisanal traditions. Many of the shops in Barrio Italia are dedicated to showcasing handmade goods, ranging from furniture and home décor to clothing and jewelry. This emphasis on craftsmanship not only supports local artisans but also invites visitors to appreciate the value of unique, high-quality products. The blend of traditional skills with modern design sensibilities has contributed to Barrio Italia's reputation as a center for innovation and creativity, making it a must-visit destination for those interested in experiencing Santiago's cultural diversity.

